.policy "ruff-pyi033-legacy-type-comment" revision 2
.description "Use inline annotations instead of type comments in stub files; type comments are deprecated and never needed in stubs."
.language python
.mode steer
.scope include "**/*"

// Ruff PYI033 (flake8-pyi), stubs only: a type comment, `# type: int`. Ruff strips `#` and leading space, takes
// what follows `type:` and reports it unless it is empty, starts with `#` right away, or starts with `ignore` after
// its leading space (`ignore[code]`, even `ignored`: a pragma). Whitespace alone after `type:` is a type comment
// to Ruff, as is `# type: #foo`. The comment must start with `type:`, so `# noqa # type: int` is not one.
//   x = 1  # type: int        ← PYI033
//   x = 1  # type: ignore     fine
#include "python/typing.rerail"

.violation PYI033(at: node) code "PYI033" "Replace this type comment with an inline annotation, such as `x: int = 1` or a per-parameter annotation; stubs never need type comments. Leave `type: ignore` comments alone."
    suppress ruff "PYI033"
PYI033(c) :- kind(c, "comment"), match("#\\s*type:[^#].*", c), !match("#\\s*type:\\s*ignore.*", c), in_stub(c).
